---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteScripts from '../components/SiteScripts.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL } from '../data/site';
import { LOGO_PATH } from '../data/brand';

const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'feedback@plozz.app';
const SENTRY_PRIVACY_URL = 'https://sentry.io/privacy/';
const GITHUB_PRIVACY_URL = 'https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement';
const LAST_UPDATED = 'October 26, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Plozz"
  description="How Plozz handles server logins, iCloud sync, approved device setup, connected services and optional crash reports. No Plozz account or usage analytics."
>
  <main class="legal">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="legal-home" href="/">
        <img src={LOGO_PATH} alt="" width="28" height="28" />
        <span>Plozz</span>
      </a>

      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

      <p>
        Plozz is a media player for Apple TV, iPhone and iPad. It connects to
        Jellyfin, Plex, Emby, Silo and network shares that you choose.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Plozz has no usage analytics and no Plozz account. Crash reporting is
        optional and requires your sharing choice. Playing media, fetching metadata,
        syncing settings and using connected services still require network
        requests. Those connections are described below; “no analytics”
        doesn’t mean the app never communicates with another service.
      </p>

      <h2>Crash reports &amp; diagnostics (optional)</h2>
      <p>
        Current builds ask you to choose{' '}
        <strong>Share Diagnostics</strong> or <strong>Don’t Share</strong>.
        Either choice lets you continue setup. Reporting stays off until you
        choose to share, and you can change the choice in Help &amp; Diagnostics.
        Consent belongs to this device; it is not synced or transferred.
      </p>
      <p>
        When enabled, automatic reports can include crash stacks, technical
        errors, app and device information, fixed screen categories, and
        performance measurements. Plozz filters account identity, request
        information and arbitrary log text from these events before submission.
        This does not make a promise of complete anonymity: the receiving
        service also processes the network connection used to send the report.
      </p>
      <p>
        While crash reporting is turned on, you can also tap{' '}
        <strong>“Send to Developer”</strong> in Help &amp; Diagnostics or Recent
        Activity to submit technical evidence and an optional message. Structured
        reports contain activity categories and severity, relative timings,
        and filtered playback, connection, library and source records—not the
        original recent-activity messages. Record identifiers are replaced with
        fresh labels for that report. Your optional message is sent as written;
        don’t include passwords or other information you don’t want to share.
        Nothing is sent by this action unless you press the button.
      </p>
      <p id="build-differences">
        <strong>Build differences:</strong> older beta builds can send the
        original recent activity log instead of a structured report. Those
        logs can contain server addresses, account or media identifiers,
        titles and search text. Review the activity shown in your installed
        build before choosing to send it. Legacy builds may also have different
        diagnostics defaults; check their Help &amp; Diagnostics setting.
      </p>
      <p>
        Crash reports and diagnostics are processed and stored by our
        error-monitoring provider,{' '}
        <a href={SENTRY_PRIVACY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sentry</a>{' '}
        (Functional Software, Inc.), on servers in the United States, under
        Sentry’s privacy policy.         You can turn sharing off at any time in the app, which disables
        automatic reporting and the “Send to Developer” button.
      </p>

      <h2>Bug reports &amp; feedback</h2>
      <p>
        When you choose to report a problem from inside Plozz, the app shows a
        link and QR code that open a pre-filled issue on our public{' '}
        <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/issues`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>{' '}
        repository — only you decide whether to submit it. The pre-filled text
        can include your app and operating-system versions, device model,
        connected provider types and activity details. Builds with structured
        exports use activity categories and severity instead of raw log messages;
        older beta builds can include a log excerpt. Review the pre-filled text
        before posting. Anything you submit—including your GitHub identity and
        text you add—is public and handled under{' '}
        <a href={GITHUB_PRIVACY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub’s privacy policy</a>.
        You can also email us at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; we only receive
        what you choose to send.
      </p>

      <h2>Your server details</h2>
      <p>
        Media-server credentials are stored in the system Keychain and authorize
        connections to the services you choose. They are not sent to the
        developer as part of connecting to your media server. Eligible sign-ins
        can transfer through the sync and device-setup paths below.
        Server users retain their server-owned access restrictions and watch
        history; local Plozz profiles don’t replace those identities.
      </p>

      <h2>iCloud and setting up another device</h2>
      <p>
        When enabled, iCloud Sync can carry profiles, preferences, server
        descriptors, watchlist state, supported Live TV configuration and
        tracker sign-ins through your Apple account. Configuration is stored
        in the app’s private CloudKit database; credential-bearing tracker
        and supported Live TV records use encrypted storage.
        This sync does not transfer movies or offline downloads.
      </p>
      <p>
        With sync and iCloud Keychain available, iPhone and iPad can also
        transfer supported Jellyfin, Plex, Emby, network-share and Seerr
        sign-ins. Apple TV does not use that iCloud Keychain credential path;
        sign in there or use approved device setup. Not every credential is
        transferable, and device-local generated SSH keys remain local.
        See <a href="https://docs.plozz.app/profiles-and-sync/">Profiles and sync</a>{' '}
        for current platform and provider limits.
      </p>
      <p>
        Supported tracker sign-ins can also sync through iCloud Keychain on
        iPhone and iPad when Apple’s iCloud Keychain is enabled, independently
        of Plozz’s iCloud Sync setting.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you approve device-to-device setup, eligible providers’ login
        credentials can transfer through that flow. Silo is an exception:
        its rotating login is never cloned. Only the server descriptor transfers,
        and the receiving device must pair with Silo independently. Pending Silo
        setup remains available in Settings → iCloud Sync.
      </p>

      <h2>Network connections</h2>
      <p>
        Plozz connects to your configured media servers and network shares
        for libraries, playback, subtitles and downloads. Providers receive
        the authentication and playback information needed to supply those
        features. Data handling on those servers is governed by their
        operators’ policies. Connections expose network information such as
        your IP address to the recipient. Plex and Jellyfin-compatible
        connections also identify the client using a stored device identifier.
      </p>
      <p>
        Artwork, metadata, ratings and subtitle lookups can contact the
        services configured for those features. Connected trackers such as
        Trakt, AniList, MyAnimeList, Simkl, Last.fm and WeTrakr receive the supported
        watchlist or listening/watching activity you enable. Seerr receives
        requests using the linked server user. These services can retain
        account-linked activity and use it according to their own privacy
        policies, including their personalization or analytics practices.
        Connecting a service is not the same as sending activity to a
        Plozz-operated analytics service.
      </p>
      <h2>Website authorization and pairing</h2>
      <p>
        The website hosts the authorization relay used to connect AniList and
        MyAnimeList. It temporarily processes authorization tokens and session
        data so another device can finish sign-in. Those application records
        are configured to expire after ten minutes, and redeemed token records
        are deleted after use. Failed redemption attempts create IP-keyed
        security counters configured to expire after ten minutes.
      </p>
      <p>
        PublicMetaDB browser pairing transfers a key to the requesting device.
        The browser encrypts the key before sending it to the relay. Temporary
        state contains public keys, the encrypted message, a hash of the app’s
        redemption secret and pairing status. The encrypted message is removed
        after redemption or cancellation; pairing state expires after ten minutes.
        Hashed-IP rate-limit records also expire after ten minutes. The website
        supplies the encryption code and remains a trusted part of this flow.
      </p>
      <p>
        Infrastructure logs follow the hosting provider’s data-handling policies.
        The website is hosted by Cloudflare and requests the public GitHub star
        count from GitHub.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Plozz is a general-purpose media player. Parents and guardians should
        choose suitable media sources and review diagnostics-sharing choices
        on devices used by children. See{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.plozz.app/parental-controls/">Parental controls</a>{' '}
        for setup and limitations.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy; changes will be posted at this URL.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
  <SiteScripts />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding: 64px 0 88px;
  }

  .legal .container {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .legal-home {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    font-weight: var(--w-strong);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    transition: color 0.15s ease;
  }

  .legal-home:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .legal-home img {
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    image-rendering: pixelated;
  }

  .legal h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.8rem);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }

  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin-top: 36px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .legal p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--brand);
  }

  .legal a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
